  "visual_observations": {
    "source": "Canonical Ghost Library still. One candle / skeleton / shelf edge per feature. JPEG softness is not Camotion ghost-copy.",
    "01_strong_exposure": "Discrete repeated copies appear along the radial trajectory on candles, shelf edges, and skeleton structure.",
    "02_medium_exposure": "The same features also show discrete copies, with shorter streaks than strong.",
    "13_strong_plus_medium": "Foreground artifact crops are byte-identical to 16. Mixing strong+medium does not introduce a new first appearance; both layers already contain copies.",
    "16_full_depth_banded": "Foreground artifact crops contain the repeated-object appearance before route preservation. Pristine weight is 0.0 in those four crops.",
    "mid_left_candle": "This mid-aisle crop is the exception: pristine is materially active (all-three fraction 0.131). 13 vs 16 MAE 18.6. Route then changes this crop (MAE 0.85). First ghost copies are still visible in strong exposure here.",
    "17_route_preserved": "left-skeleton, left-lower-candle, right-skeleton, and right-lower-candle are byte-identical to 16. Route is not the source of those copies.",
    "18_final_01_8": "Destination protection is byte-identical to 17 in all five diagnostic crops. Destination bbox vs source is identical. PNG matches committed 01.8.",
